Bounded model checking of USB driver error paths with CBMC.

Needs cbmc (tested with 5.95.1) and gcc on the build host.  The kernel
sources are preprocessed with a minimal stand-in for a compile directory,
so no config(8) run is needed.

	sh cbmc.sh usps

prints one of:

	RESULT: VERIFIED	no memory-safety violation within the bounds
	RESULT: VIOLATED	a violation was found; see check.out
	RESULT: VACUOUS		an anchor in must_reach was not reachable
	RESULT: ERROR		build or tool failure

What is modelled
	- real bodies of the functions listed in <target>/keep
	- functions in <target>/nobody return any value, no side effects
	- every other function loses its body
	- malloc(9)/free(9) map to CBMC's heap (common/stubs_alloc.c);
	  M_NOWAIT allocations may fail
	- the harness supplies the host controller methods and the device
	- bus and pipe method calls are bound to those methods
	  (common/fptargets), so a call through a freed pipe's method
	  table is reported as a bad dereference but not followed

What is not modelled
	- interrupts, other threads, locks
	- transfers actually queued on a pipe

Adding a target
	1. Copy usps/ to <driver>/.
	2. harness.c: build the softc and attach arguments the driver's
	   entry point expects, call the entry point, then call the
	   function that runs on unplug or close.
	3. sources, keep: the driver file and the functions on the path.
	4. must_reach: one anchor inside the error path under test and one
	   in the teardown function.
	5. opts: every loop on the path needs a bound at least as large as
	   its trip count; --unwinding-assertions reports one that is not.

Rules for a harness
	- no __CPROVER_assume
	- do not add driver or usbdi functions to nobody to make a
	  failure go away; nobody is for hardware and request I/O
	- a VERIFIED result counts only together with must_reach anchors
	  on the error path

Targets
	usps	usps_attach followed by usps_detach.  With usbd_open_pipe_intr
		storing *pipe before checking usbd_transfer's result this
		target is VIOLATED (the freed pipe is closed again by
		usps_attach and by usps_detach).
	umcs	umcs_attach followed by umcs_detach.
	uow	uow_attach followed by uow_detach.  uow_cmd is not in keep:
		its retry loop waits for a status byte that only the
		interrupt handler updates, so it has no bound in this model.
	ubcmtp	ubcmtp_setup_pipes followed by ubcmtp_disable on a softc
		built by hand; the softc definition is copied from ubcmtp.c
		and has to be kept in sync with it.
